# CTT: stable symlink for the Telit LE910Q1 (1bc7:7021) AT control port (USB
# interface 02): /dev/ctt-modem-at.
#
# ModemManager uses interface 02 as the modem's AT port (signal/registration),
# and it floats across /dev/ttyACMx between boots, so we give it a fixed name.
# That fixed name is what ctt-modem-provision binds the ECM data path on: it
# starts the CDC-ECM session (AT#ECM=1,0) at boot, which — unlike the old RNDIS
# NV binding — does not persist across a modem power-cycle and must be re-issued
# every boot (ctt-modem-provision.service, ordered Before=ModemManager).
#
# Telit-VID scoped (1bc7:7021) — Quectel/QMI and every other device is untouched.
# Interface 02 is the AT control port in both the RNDIS (7020) and ECM (7021)
# compositions, so only the product id changes here.
#
# Match on the tty's own ID_* properties (set by the usb_id builtin in the
# earlier 60-serial rules), NOT ATTRS{}: idVendor/idProduct live on the USB
# device while bInterfaceNumber lives on the interface — different parents, and
# udev requires all ATTRS{} in one rule to match the SAME parent, so an ATTRS
# matcher can never match all three. ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM=="02" selects the AT
# control port (ModemManager's primary AT port).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="1bc7", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="7021", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", SYMLINK+="ctt-modem-at"
